e at 08:42:28 and pushed at 08:45:34; a local session ran COMPACT at 08:44:05, enumerating fold inputs before the bridge push merged; the union merge then landed the comment file into a dir whose snapshot postdates it. Result: no file loss, but the reducer's replay (snapshot + post-snapshot events) skips the comment — it is INVISIBLE in `rebar show` (verified: 16 comments rendered, orphan absent) while existing on disk and in Jira. The crash-atomic fold (compulsory-pernickety-mantis, merged) is orthogonal: journaling/rollback protects against interrupted folds, not against concurrent remote arrivals; `compact` also refuses a manual re-fold here (\"remote SNAPSHOT exists\" guard), so today there is NO supported repair door for this class.\n\n## Proposed fix\nTwo-sided, portable (no CI dependency):\n1) **Self-heal at read/fold time**: teach the fold (and/or reducer) that an unretired event older than the active snapshot but missing from `source_event_uuids` is a LATE ARRIVAL, not noise — fold it into the next snapshot (re-fold absorbing orphans) or replay it after the snapshot despite its timestamp (stable order: snapshot, then orphans by ts, then post-snapshot events). Choose ONE semantics and pin it with tests; re-fold is preferred because it also clears the fsck finding.\n2) **Repair door**: `rebar doctor --repair` handles ORPHAN_EVENT by triggering that absorbing re-fold under the store write lock (compact's \"remote SNAPSHOT exists\" refusal must not block the doctor path; doctor passes an explicit absorb flag). Backup ref before mutation, mirroring the dirty-tracker repair envelope (change 1771).\n\n## Scope\n- Fold/enumeration seam in src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py (+ compact.py guard) — absorb-orphans path.\n- Reducer replay seam if option (replay) chosen instead.\n- src/rebar/_commands/doctor.py — ORPHAN_EVENT repair routing.\n- Tests: fold-race reproduction (event file lands post-enumeration pre-commit via union merge), absorbing re-fold clears fsck and restores comment visibility in show; guard test that a genuinely retired-and-folded event is NOT re-absorbed.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] A reproduced fold-race orphan is visible in `rebar show` after the repair, and fsck reports 0 ORPHAN_EVENT for the ticket; new integration test.\n- [ ] `rebar doctor --repair` clears ORPHAN_EVENT via absorbing re-fold with a backup ref; unit test.\n- [ ] A retired event already in `source_event_uuids` is never re-absorbed; guard test.\n- [ ] `make lint`/`make typecheck` clean; lands via Gerrit (LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1) before close.\n\n## Out of scope\nBridge/Jira duplicate-comment reconciliation policy; crash-atomicity (landed with mantis); dirty-tree repair (landed with dormouse 1771).","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py","reason":"absorbing re-fold: enumeration treats unretired pre-snapshot events missing from source_event_uuids as late arrivals"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/compact.py","reason":"remote-SNAPSHOT refusal must not block the explicit absorb path"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/doctor.py","reason":"ORPHAN_EVENT repair routing under write lock with backup ref"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/fsck.py","reason":"finding must clear after absorbing re-fold; JSON registration reused"},{"path":"tests/integration/test_fold_race_orphan.py","reason":"new: fold-race reproduction + repair round-trip"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_doctor_orphan_repair.py","reason":"new: doctor routing + backup ref + guard tests"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"40a278b1-353c-4b02-9a77-24a00fa7e9ad","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"f96b-3498-8f04-40b0","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Fold-horizon race: concurrent remote write during compact leaves ORPHAN_EVENT invisible to replay; no repair door","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["eadc4184-1c01-4aea-b830-1919d1bdbeda","e8ac1c45-de82-4755-96ee-bef21e33d3b9","40a278b1-353c-4b02-9a77-24a00fa7e9ad","cd9201f0-c76d-47c0-8356-f6b7fccd3e72","749cd8f5-c39e-4a5b-a8e0-dc476202537e"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786722941614315002,"uuid":"dc65c513-b3cd-43f3-88d6-93842e5f5d2d"}